<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Algorithm</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide the complete algorithmic specification of AceMAD in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix A Algorithm ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. The protocol operationalizes the theoretical framework developed in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Theoretical Framework ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> through a four-phase iterative process: (1) Argumentation, where agents generate natural language arguments; (2) Signal Extraction, where agents commit to both self-beliefs and peer-predictions; (3) Verification, where the Brier score quantifies cognitive potential; and (4) Non-linear Amplification, where exponential weight updates convert this potential into submartingale drift. The final decision aggregates beliefs using squared weights to further amplify the truth-holder’s influence.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> AceMAD</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Query <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, Set of Agents <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, Rounds <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, Rate <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialize:</span> Weights <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}^{(0)}\leftarrow 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}^{(0)}\leftarrow 1</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Initialize:</span> History <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(0)}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(0)}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each agent <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> in parallel <span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
             Generate argument <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> based on <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(t-1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
             Commit Self-Belief <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and Peer-Forecast <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{q}_{i}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{q}_{i}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
            Update History <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{(t)}\leftarrow H^{(t-1)}\cup\{m_{1}^{(t)},\dots,m_{N}^{(t)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{(t)}\leftarrow H^{(t-1)}\cup\{m_{1}^{(t)},\dots,m_{N}^{(t)}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each agent <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
            
            
             Calculate peer realization <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{Q}_{-i}^{(t)}\leftarrow\frac{1}{N-1}\sum_{j\neq i}p_{j}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{Q}_{-i}^{(t)}\leftarrow\frac{1}{N-1}\sum_{j\neq i}p_{j}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
            
            
             Compute score <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}^{(t)}\leftarrow 1-||\hat{q}_{i}^{(t)}-\bar{Q}_{-i}^{(t)}||_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}^{(t)}\leftarrow 1-||\hat{q}_{i}^{(t)}-\bar{Q}_{-i}^{(t)}||_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
            
            
             Update weight <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}^{(t)}\leftarrow w_{i}^{(t-1)}\cdot\exp(\eta\cdot S_{i}^{(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}^{(t)}\leftarrow w_{i}^{(t-1)}\cdot\exp(\eta\cdot S_{i}^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
            
            
            Normalize weights <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w^{(t)}\leftarrow w^{(t)}/\sum_{j}w_{j}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w^{(t)}\leftarrow w^{(t)}/\sum_{j}w_{j}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Return</span> <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max_{y}\sum_{i}(w_{i}^{(T)})^{2}p_{i}^{(T)}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi>y</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max_{y}\sum_{i}(w_{i}^{(T)})^{2}p_{i}^{(T)}(y)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Implementation</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All experiments are conducted using the same base infrastructure to ensure fair comparison. We implement AceMAD using the following configuration:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">(1) <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model Selection</span>: We primarily use <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GPT-4o-mini</span> as our base model, with additional validation on <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen3-235B-A22B-Instruct</span>, <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DeepSeek-V3.1</span>, and <span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct</span> to verify generalization across architectures.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">(2) <span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hyperparameters</span>: The amplification rate <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is set to 2.0 across all experiments unless otherwise specified. We found this value provides sufficient signal amplification while maintaining numerical stability.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">(3) <span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Agent Configuration</span>: Following Section <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Inducing Agent Heterogeneity ‣ 5 The AceMAD Protocol ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, we induce heterogeneity through a dual-strategy approach in main experiment:</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Crowd agents (80% of the group): Temperature = 0.1, configured to approximate maximum likelihood behavior</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Truth-holder agents (20% of the group): Temperature = 0.6, assigned critical-thinking personas to explore distributional tails</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Challenging Subset Construction</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each benchmark, we construct the <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Challenging Interval subset<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">1</span></span>
                
                
                
                
                
                
                
              <span id="footnote1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">We will release our challenging subsets for all benchmarks.</span></span></span></span></span> by filtering instances where a naive single-agent baseline (Temperature = 0.7) consistently fails. Specifically:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">1. Run the single-agent baseline 5 times on each instance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">2. Select instances where accuracy <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&lt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;</annotation></semantics></math>40% across runs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">3. Manually verify that failures are due to systematic misconceptions rather than random errors.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">4. The resulting subsets is the challenging subset.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This construction ensures we evaluate debate mechanisms precisely in the Challenging Interval where they should prove most valuable.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Evaluation Metrics</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report <span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">accuracy</span> as the primary metric, computed as the proportion of instances where the final aggregated decision matches the ground truth. For MAD variants, the final decision is determined by weighted voting (Eq. <a href="#S5.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ 5.1 Protocol Design ‣ 5 The AceMAD Protocol ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>). For majority voting, we use simple plurality among initial responses.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Benchmarks</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate AceMAD across six diverse benchmarks, each targeting different aspects of challenging reasoning. These benchmarks are specifically chosen because they expose common failure modes in LLMs: systematic biases, logical traps, and domain-specific misconceptions. Below we provide detailed descriptions of each benchmark and explain why they are particularly suitable for evaluating debate mechanisms in the Challenging Interval:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TruthfulQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite> is a benchmark designed to evaluate the truthfulness of LLMs, comprising 817 questions across 38 categories such as health, law, and finance. It is specifically constructed to induce models into generating false answers that mimic common human misconceptions, thereby assessing the model’s ability to avoid hallucinations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ARC-Challenge</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> focuses on grade-school science questions, with the Challenge subset strictly containing problems that retrieval-based or co-occurrence algorithms fail to answer. It requires models to possess not only scientific common sense but also deep reasoning capabilities to understand underlying physical processes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">BBH</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> (BIG-bench Hard) is a curated suite of 23 challenging tasks selected from BIG-bench where LLMs typically perform below the average human rater. It is designed to stress-test advanced reasoning abilities across diverse settings, including multi-step reasoning, symbolic manipulation, and complex logical structures.We chose the logic-related subset.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LogiQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>, sourced from the National Civil Servants Examination of China, contains truth-holder-level logical reasoning and reading comprehension problems. It covers various forms of reasoning, including deductive and inductive logic, requiring models to extract logical relationships from complex texts for deep analysis.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MedQA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite> is a large-scale biomedical question-answering dataset collected from medical licensing exams in the US (USMLE), Mainland China, and Taiwan. It benchmarks the model’s proficiency in broad medical knowledge, clinical case analysis, and diagnostic reasoning within medical contexts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MMLU-Pro (Law)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite> is a robust version of the classic MMLU benchmark, designed to rigorously evaluate reasoning by increasing difficulty, removing noise, and expanding the option set. The Law subset specifically tests the model’s mastery of complex legal provisions, case analysis, and jurisprudential logic.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Baselines</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare AceMAD against four baseline approaches that represent different paradigms in Multi-Agent Debate. These baselines span the spectrum from zero-interaction ensemble methods (Majority Voting) to various MAD architectures with different communication topologies. Below we provide precise specifications of each baseline to ensure reproducibility and fair comparison:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Decentralized MAD</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">49</a>]</cite> adopts a fully connected communication topology. In each round of debate, every agent receives the complete history of responses from all other peer agents to update their own reasoning and answers, facilitating comprehensive information exchange across the entire collective.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Sparse MAD</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">37</a>]</cite> is a variant of the decentralized framework designed to enhance computational efficiency. It utilizes a sparse communication topology where each agent interacts with only a limited subset of peers rather than the entire group, significantly reducing the information exchange overhead while maintaining collaborative reasoning.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Centralized MAD</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> employs a star topology with a designated central agent or moderator. In this setup, the central agent is responsible for aggregating responses from all peer agents and generating a unified updated answer or summary at each debate round, acting as the primary bottleneck for information synthesis.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Majority Voting</span> serves as a non-debate baseline that aggregates the initial zero-shot responses from multiple independent agents. The final answer is selected based on the most frequent prediction (consensus), which allows us to isolate the performance gains attributed specifically to the iterative multi-agent debate mechanism.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Setup and Challenging Interval Formulation</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider a single binary prediction task with ground truth</p>
<table id="A5.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\in\{0,1\},\qquad\mathbb{P}(Y=1)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\in\{0,1\},\qquad\mathbb{P}(Y=1)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">There are <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> agents. One of them is an truth-holder <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> who possesses asymmetric cognitive potential energy, and the remaining <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-1</annotation></semantics></math> agents form the hallucinating majority <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> suffering from common misconceptions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At round <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, each agent <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,\dots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,\dots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math> holds a subjective belief</p>
<table id="A5.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{(t)}:=P_{i}^{(t)}(Y=1)\in[0,1]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{(t)}:=P_{i}^{(t)}(Y=1)\in[0,1].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In the correlated noise regime, we assume that the truth-holder is systematically closer to the truth than the crowd:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{E}^{(t)}\approx 1-\delta,\qquad p_{c}^{(t)}\approx\varepsilon\quad\text{for all }c\in C," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≈</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{E}^{(t)}\approx 1-\delta,\qquad p_{c}^{(t)}\approx\varepsilon\quad\text{for all }c\in C,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\varepsilon\in(0,1/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\varepsilon\in(0,1/2)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> represents the truth-holder’s small error margin and <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> represents the crowd’s persistent bias toward the incorrect answer.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In each round, the AceMAD protocol proceeds as follows:</p>
<ol id="A5.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Argue.</span> Agents produce natural-language arguments based on the debate history.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Commit.</span> Each agent privately commits to</p>
<ul id="A5.I1.i2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">its own belief <math id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> over answers, and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">a <em id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">peer prediction</em> <math id="A5.I1.i2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{Q}_{i}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{Q}_{i}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a prediction of the empirical mean of the other agents’ reported beliefs.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reveal &amp; score.</span> All commitments are revealed. For each agent <math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute the realized average of others’ reports,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{Q}_{-i}^{(t)}:=\frac{1}{N-1}\sum_{j\neq i}P_{j}^{(t)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{Q}_{-i}^{(t)}:=\frac{1}{N-1}\sum_{j\neq i}P_{j}^{(t)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and assign a Brier-type peer prediction score</p>
<table id="A5.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}^{(t)}:=1-\bigl\|\hat{Q}_{i}^{(t)}-\bar{Q}_{-i}^{(t)}\bigr\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}^{(t)}:=1-\bigl\|\hat{Q}_{i}^{(t)}-\bar{Q}_{-i}^{(t)}\bigr\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Update.</span> We maintain non-negative weights <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{i}^{(t)}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{i}^{(t)}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. At the end of round <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, weights are updated multiplicatively:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}^{(t+1)}=w_{i}^{(t)}\cdot\exp\bigl(\eta S_{i}^{(t)}\bigr)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}^{(t+1)}=w_{i}^{(t)}\cdot\exp\bigl(\eta S_{i}^{(t)}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a learning-rate parameter.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Aggregate.</span> The aggregated belief at round <math id="A5.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the weight-averaged belief</p>
<table id="A5.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1):=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{i}^{(t)}\,p_{i}^{(t)}}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{j}^{(t)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1):=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}w_{i}^{(t)}\,p_{i}^{(t)}}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}w_{j}^{(t)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We show that:</p>
<ol id="A5.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The AceMAD channel Blackwell-dominates standard debate (Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 4.2 (Information-Theoretic Manifestation of Cognitive Potential). ‣ Interpretation. ‣ 4.1 Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy in MAD ‣ 4 Theoretical Framework ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The truth-holder achieves a strictly higher expected peer-prediction score than the crowd (Theorem <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem E.3 (Identification via proper scoring). ‣ E.3 Cognitive Potential Energy Separation ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>);</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under multiplicative weight updates, the aggregated belief <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)</annotation></semantics></math> forms a sub-martingale with a positive drift towards the truth (Theorem <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem E.6 (Breaking the Martingale Curse: positive drift). ‣ E.4 Converting Potential Energy into Submartingale Drift ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.6</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Information-Theoretic Manifestation</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We view both standard debate and AceMAD as information channels from the ground truth <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> to observable transcripts.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathrm{std}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>std</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathrm{std}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the channel corresponding to standard multi-agent debate. On each instance, it outputs the transcript</p>
<table id="A5.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\mathrm{std}}=\bigl(A_{i}^{(t)},P_{i}^{(t)}\bigr)_{i=1}^{N}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>std</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\mathrm{std}}=\bigl(A_{i}^{(t)},P_{i}^{(t)}\bigr)_{i=1}^{N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> are the arguments and <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{i}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{i}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> the self-beliefs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathrm{info}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>info</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathrm{info}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the AceMAD channel. Its transcript is</p>
<table id="A5.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\mathrm{info}}=\bigl(A_{i}^{(t)},P_{i}^{(t)},\hat{Q}_{i}^{(t)},S_{i}^{(t)}\bigr)_{i=1}^{N}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>info</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\mathrm{info}}=\bigl(A_{i}^{(t)},P_{i}^{(t)},\hat{Q}_{i}^{(t)},S_{i}^{(t)}\bigr)_{i=1}^{N},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">which strictly contains the standard transcript plus peer forecasts and scores.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We recall the Blackwell order on channels: for two channels <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> to outputs <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we say that <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> Blackwell-dominates <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> if there exists a stochastic kernel <math id="A5.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}=\kappa\circ\sigma_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}=\kappa\circ\sigma_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Blackwell dominance of AceMAD)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a stochastic kernel <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathrm{std}}=\kappa\circ\sigma_{\mathrm{info}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>std</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>info</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathrm{std}}=\kappa\circ\sigma_{\mathrm{info}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Hence, AceMAD Blackwell-dominates standard debate. Moreover, in the correlated noise regime, this dominance is strict.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the projection</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:Z_{\mathrm{info}}\mapsto Z_{\mathrm{std}},\qquad f\bigl((A_{i},P_{i},\hat{Q}_{i},S_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\bigr):=(A_{i},P_{i})_{i=1}^{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>info</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>std</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:Z_{\mathrm{info}}\mapsto Z_{\mathrm{std}},\qquad f\bigl((A_{i},P_{i},\hat{Q}_{i},S_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\bigr):=(A_{i},P_{i})_{i=1}^{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">This projection simply discards peer forecasts and scores. We can turn <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> into a deterministic stochastic kernel <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> by setting</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa(z_{\mathrm{std}}\mid z_{\mathrm{info}}):=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if }z_{\mathrm{std}}=f(z_{\mathrm{info}}),\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>std</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>info</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>std</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>info</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa(z_{\mathrm{std}}\mid z_{\mathrm{info}}):=\begin{cases}1,&amp;\text{if }z_{\mathrm{std}}=f(z_{\mathrm{info}}),\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">By construction, sampling <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z_{\mathrm{info}}\sim\sigma_{\mathrm{info}}(\cdot\mid Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>info</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>info</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\mathrm{info}}\sim\sigma_{\mathrm{info}}(\cdot\mid Y)</annotation></semantics></math> and then applying <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> yields exactly the same distribution over <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\mathrm{std}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>std</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\mathrm{std}}</annotation></semantics></math> as sampling directly from <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{\mathrm{std}}(\cdot\mid Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>std</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathrm{std}}(\cdot\mid Y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\mathrm{std}}=\kappa\circ\sigma_{\mathrm{info}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>std</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>info</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\mathrm{std}}=\kappa\circ\sigma_{\mathrm{info}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which shows that AceMAD Blackwell-dominates standard debate in the weak sense.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">To see that the dominance is strict in the correlated noise regime, consider the decision problem of selecting a single agent whose prediction will be used as the final report. Under AceMAD, the scores <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{S_{i}^{(t)}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{S_{i}^{(t)}\}</annotation></semantics></math> reveal which agent is systematically better at forecasting peers (Theorem <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem E.3 (Identification via proper scoring). ‣ E.3 Cognitive Potential Energy Separation ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>), allowing a decision-maker to allocate more weight to the truth-holder and achieve lower Bayes risk in predicting <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>. Under standard debate, the scores are not observable, and in the correlated noise regime arguments and self-beliefs alone do not suffice to reliably identify the truth-holder. Therefore, there exists at least one decision problem (namely, choosing which agent to follow) for which AceMAD yields a strictly lower expected loss than standard debate. This implies strict Blackwell dominance.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Cognitive Potential Energy Separation </h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now show that, under the correlated noise assumptions and a strictly proper scoring rule, the truth-holder obtains a strictly higher expected peer-prediction score than the crowd.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We model the realized average of other agents’ reports as a random probability vector. Fix an agent <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, and let</p>
<table id="A5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X:=\bar{Q}_{-i}^{(t)}\in\Delta(\mathcal{A})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X:=\bar{Q}_{-i}^{(t)}\in\Delta(\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">denote the empirical distribution over a finite answer set <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. An agent reports a forecast <math id="A5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\Delta(\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\Delta(\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is scored by the Brier score</p>
<table id="A5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(q,X):=1-\|q-X\|_{2}^{2}=1-\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}(q_{a}-X_{a})^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>a</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(q,X):=1-\|q-X\|_{2}^{2}=1-\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}(q_{a}-X_{a})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We first recall a standard decomposition of squared error.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Brier decomposition)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> be a random vector in <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> with mean <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:=\mathbb{E}[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:=\mathbb{E}[X]</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|q-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|X-\mu\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]+\|q-\mu\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|q-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|X-\mu\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]+\|q-\mu\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write <math id="A5.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q-X\|_{2}^{2}=\sum_{k=1}^{d}(q_{k}-X_{k})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q-X\|_{2}^{2}=\sum_{k=1}^{d}(q_{k}-X_{k})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each coordinate,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex17X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[(q_{k}-X_{k})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[(q_{k}-X_{k})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex17X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(X_{k}-\mu_{k}+\mu_{k}-q_{k})^{2}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(X_{k}-\mu_{k}+\mu_{k}-q_{k})^{2}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex17Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(X_{k}-\mu_{k})^{2}\bigr]+2(\mu_{k}-q_{k})\,\mathbb{E}[X_{k}-\mu_{k}]+(\mu_{k}-q_{k})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(X_{k}-\mu_{k})^{2}\bigr]+2(\mu_{k}-q_{k})\,\mathbb{E}[X_{k}-\mu_{k}]+(\mu_{k}-q_{k})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex17Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex17Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(X_{k}-\mu_{k})^{2}\bigr]+(\mu_{k}-q_{k})^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\bigl[(X_{k}-\mu_{k})^{2}\bigr]+(\mu_{k}-q_{k})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A5.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X_{k}-\mu_{k}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X_{k}-\mu_{k}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Summing over all coordinates yields</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|q-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|X-\mu\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]+\|q-\mu\|_{2}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|q-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|X-\mu\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]+\|q-\mu\|_{2}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">This shows that, in expectation, the Brier score is uniquely maximized by reporting the true mean <math id="A5.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We now apply this to the truth-holder and the crowd.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.3</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Identification via proper scoring)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X:=\bar{Q}_{-i}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X:=\bar{Q}_{-i}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the random average of other agents’ reports, with mean <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu:=\mathbb{E}[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu:=\mathbb{E}[X]</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume the truth-holder <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> has a correct probabilistic model of <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore reports <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{Q}_{E}^{(t)}=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{Q}_{E}^{(t)}=\mu</annotation></semantics></math> as its peer-forecast, while any crowd member <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in C</annotation></semantics></math> reports <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}\neq\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}\neq\mu</annotation></semantics></math> with positive probability. Then, for the Brier score,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{E}^{(t)}\bigr]&gt;\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{c}^{(t)}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{E}^{(t)}\bigr]&gt;\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{c}^{(t)}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall that <math id="A5.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(q,X)=1-\|q-X\|_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(q,X)=1-\|q-X\|_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the truth-holder, Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma E.2 (Brier decomposition). ‣ E.3 Cognitive Potential Energy Separation ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a> with <math id="A5.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=\mu</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{E}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|X-\mu\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{E}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|X-\mu\|_{2}^{2}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">For a crowd member <math id="A5.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|X-\mu\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]+\bigl\|\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}-\mu\bigr\|_{2}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|X-\mu\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]+\bigl\|\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}-\mu\bigr\|_{2}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">again by Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma E.2 (Brier decomposition). ‣ E.3 Cognitive Potential Energy Separation ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a>. Since <math id="A5.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}\neq\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≠</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}\neq\mu</annotation></semantics></math> with positive probability, we have <math id="A5.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}-\mu\bigr\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}-\mu\bigr\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]&gt;\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{E}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]&gt;\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{E}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Translating back to scores,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex23X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex23X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{E}^{(t)}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{E}^{(t)}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex23X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{E}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{E}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex23Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex23Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{c}^{(t)}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{c}^{(t)}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex23Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1-\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">so</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{E}^{(t)}\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{c}^{(t)}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{E}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{E}^{(t)}\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{c}^{(t)}\bigr]=\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{c}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]-\mathbb{E}\bigl[\|\hat{Q}_{E}^{(t)}-X\|_{2}^{2}\bigr]&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Converting Potential Energy into Submartingale Drift</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now show that, under multiplicative weight updates and the score separation of Theorem <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem E.3 (Identification via proper scoring). ‣ E.3 Cognitive Potential Energy Separation ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>, the aggregated belief <math id="A5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)</annotation></semantics></math> forms a sub-martingale with a positive drift towards the truth-holder’s belief.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For clarity, we first analyze a reduced system with two meta-agents:</p>
<ul id="A5.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the truth-holder <math id="A5.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math>, with belief <math id="A5.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{E}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{E}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">a meta-crowd <math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>, aggregating all crowd agents into a single agent with belief <math id="A5.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{C}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{C}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A5.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The general case with <math id="A5.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math> agents follows by grouping all crowd weights into a single meta-agent.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{E}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{E}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{C}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{C}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> be their weights at round <math id="A5.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the truth-holder’s weight share</p>
<table id="A5.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}^{(t)}:=\frac{w_{E}^{(t)}}{w_{E}^{(t)}+w_{C}^{(t)}},\qquad\alpha_{C}^{(t)}:=1-\alpha_{E}^{(t)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}^{(t)}:=\frac{w_{E}^{(t)}}{w_{E}^{(t)}+w_{C}^{(t)}},\qquad\alpha_{C}^{(t)}:=1-\alpha_{E}^{(t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The aggregate belief is</p>
<table id="A5.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{w}^{(t)}:=p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)=\alpha_{E}^{(t)}p_{E}^{(t)}+\alpha_{C}^{(t)}p_{C}^{(t)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{w}^{(t)}:=p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)=\alpha_{E}^{(t)}p_{E}^{(t)}+\alpha_{C}^{(t)}p_{C}^{(t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Weights are updated according to</p>
<table id="A5.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}^{(t+1)}=w_{i}^{(t)}\exp\bigl(\eta S_{i}^{(t)}\bigr),\qquad i\in\{E,C\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}^{(t+1)}=w_{i}^{(t)}\exp\bigl(\eta S_{i}^{(t)}\bigr),\qquad i\in\{E,C\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A5.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}=\frac{\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\exp\bigl(\eta S_{E}^{(t)}\bigr)}{\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\exp\bigl(\eta S_{E}^{(t)}\bigr)+\alpha_{C}^{(t)}\exp\bigl(\eta S_{C}^{(t)}\bigr)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}=\frac{\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\exp\bigl(\eta S_{E}^{(t)}\bigr)}{\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\exp\bigl(\eta S_{E}^{(t)}\bigr)+\alpha_{C}^{(t)}\exp\bigl(\eta S_{C}^{(t)}\bigr)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We first observe that the truth-holder’s weight share increases exactly when its score exceeds the crowd’s.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.4</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Monotonicity of weight shares)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any fixed <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}\geq\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad S_{E}^{(t)}\geq S_{C}^{(t)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}\geq\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad S_{E}^{(t)}\geq S_{C}^{(t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}:=\alpha_{E}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}:=\alpha_{E}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{C}:=1-\alpha_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{C}:=1-\alpha_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, and write <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{E}:=S_{E}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{E}:=S_{E}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{C}:=S_{C}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{C}:=S_{C}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}=\frac{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}}}{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}}+\alpha_{C}e^{\eta S_{C}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}=\frac{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}}}{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}}+\alpha_{C}e^{\eta S_{C}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">The inequality <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}\geq\alpha_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}\geq\alpha_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}}}{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}}+\alpha_{C}e^{\eta S_{C}}}\geq\alpha_{E}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}}}{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}}+\alpha_{C}e^{\eta S_{C}}}\geq\alpha_{E}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Assuming <math id="A5.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, this can be rearranged as</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e^{\eta S_{E}}\geq\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}}+\alpha_{C}e^{\eta S_{C}}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\alpha_{C}e^{\eta S_{E}}\geq\alpha_{C}e^{\eta S_{C}}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad S_{E}\geq S_{C}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo>≥</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>S</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{\eta S_{E}}\geq\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}}+\alpha_{C}e^{\eta S_{C}}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\alpha_{C}e^{\eta S_{E}}\geq\alpha_{C}e^{\eta S_{C}}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad S_{E}\geq S_{C},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">since the exponential is strictly increasing. The converse implication follows by the same algebra.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The change in the aggregated belief can be expressed directly in terms of the change in <math id="A5.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the simplest case where <math id="A5.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{E}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{E}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{C}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{C}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> are time-invariant, we have</p>
<table id="A5.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{w}^{(t+1)}-p_{w}^{(t)}=\bigl(\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}-\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\bigr)(p_{E}-p_{C})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{w}^{(t+1)}-p_{w}^{(t)}=\bigl(\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}-\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\bigr)(p_{E}-p_{C}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Since the truth-holder is more accurate, we have <math id="A5.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{E}&gt;p_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{E}&gt;p_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the sign of <math id="A5.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{w}^{(t+1)}-p_{w}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{w}^{(t+1)}-p_{w}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> matches that of <math id="A5.SS4.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}-\alpha_{E}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}-\alpha_{E}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which by Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma E.4 (Monotonicity of weight shares). ‣ E.4 Converting Potential Energy into Submartingale Drift ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.4</span></a> matches the sign of <math id="A5.SS4.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{E}^{(t)}-S_{C}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{E}^{(t)}-S_{C}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p">We now combine this with the expected score gap.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption E.5</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Uniform score gap)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">There exists <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all rounds <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{E}^{(t)}-S_{C}^{(t)}\,\big|\,\mathcal{F}_{t}\bigr]\geq\gamma," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[S_{E}^{(t)}-S_{C}^{(t)}\,\big|\,\mathcal{F}_{t}\bigr]\geq\gamma,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the sigma-algebra generated by the history up to round <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Assumption <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem5" title="Assumption E.5 (Uniform score gap). ‣ E.4 Converting Potential Energy into Submartingale Drift ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.5</span></a> is justified in our correlated noise model by Theorem <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem E.3 (Identification via proper scoring). ‣ E.3 Cognitive Potential Energy Separation ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>: the truth-holder is strictly better at forecasting the crowd’s average reports, and the gap is uniform as long as the crowd retains a non-trivial weight share.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We can now state the main result.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.6</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Breaking the Martingale Curse: positive drift)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose Assumption <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem5" title="Assumption E.5 (Uniform score gap). ‣ E.4 Converting Potential Energy into Submartingale Drift ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.5</span></a> holds and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{E}&gt;p_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{E}&gt;p_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for sufficiently small <math id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the aggregated belief process <math id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)\}_{t\geq 0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)\}_{t\geq 0}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sub-martingale with respect to <math id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{F}_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{F}_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[p_{w}^{(t+1)}(Y=1)\,\big|\,\mathcal{F}_{t}\bigr]\geq p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[p_{w}^{(t+1)}(Y=1)\,\big|\,\mathcal{F}_{t}\bigr]\geq p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, as long as both truth-holder and crowd retain non-zero weight share, the conditional drift is strictly positive:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[p_{w}^{(t+1)}(Y=1)-p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)\,\big|\,\mathcal{F}_{t}\bigr]&gt;0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[p_{w}^{(t+1)}(Y=1)-p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)\,\big|\,\mathcal{F}_{t}\bigr]&gt;0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS4.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">We focus on the two-meta-agent reduction described above. Let us write <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}:=\alpha_{E}^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}:=\alpha_{E}^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{C}:=1-\alpha_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{C}:=1-\alpha_{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the score difference</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{(t)}:=S_{E}^{(t)}-S_{C}^{(t)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{(t)}:=S_{E}^{(t)}-S_{C}^{(t)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">From the weight update, we can express <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}=\frac{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}^{(t)}}}{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}^{(t)}}+\alpha_{C}e^{\eta S_{C}^{(t)}}}=\frac{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta D^{(t)}}}{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta D^{(t)}}+\alpha_{C}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>S</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}=\frac{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}^{(t)}}}{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta S_{E}^{(t)}}+\alpha_{C}e^{\eta S_{C}^{(t)}}}=\frac{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta D^{(t)}}}{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta D^{(t)}}+\alpha_{C}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">For fixed <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, define</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(d):=\frac{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta d}}{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta d}+\alpha_{C}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(d):=\frac{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta d}}{\alpha_{E}e^{\eta d}+\alpha_{C}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">so that <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}=g(D^{(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}=g(D^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}=g(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}=g(0)</annotation></semantics></math>. A Taylor expansion of <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> around <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=0</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(d)=g(0)+g^{\prime}(0)\,d+O(d^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(d)=g(0)+g^{\prime}(0)\,d+O(d^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">with</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\prime}(0)=\alpha_{E}\alpha_{C}\eta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\prime}(0)=\alpha_{E}\alpha_{C}\eta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p11.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p11.6.1" class="ltx_text">Since the scores are bounded, <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded, and thus <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(d^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(d^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> can be controlled uniformly. Therefore, there exists a constant <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}-\alpha_{E}\geq\alpha_{E}\alpha_{C}\eta D^{(t)}-K\eta^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}-\alpha_{E}\geq\alpha_{E}\alpha_{C}\eta D^{(t)}-K\eta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p11.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p11.7.1" class="ltx_text">for all rounds <math id="A5.SS4.p11.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assuming <math id="A5.SS4.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{E}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS4.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed across rounds, the change in the aggregated belief is</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{w}^{(t+1)}-p_{w}^{(t)}=\bigl(\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}-\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\bigr)(p_{E}-p_{C})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{w}^{(t+1)}-p_{w}^{(t)}=\bigl(\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}-\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\bigr)(p_{E}-p_{C}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking conditional expectations and applying Assumption <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem5" title="Assumption E.5 (Uniform score gap). ‣ E.4 Converting Potential Energy into Submartingale Drift ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.5</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex44X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex44X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[p_{w}^{(t+1)}-p_{w}^{(t)}\,\big|\,\mathcal{F}_{t}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigl[p_{w}^{(t+1)}-p_{w}^{(t)}\,\big|\,\mathcal{F}_{t}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex44X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(p_{E}-p_{C})\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}-\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\,\big|\,\mathcal{F}_{t}\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(p_{E}-p_{C})\,\mathbb{E}\bigl[\alpha_{E}^{(t+1)}-\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\,\big|\,\mathcal{F}_{t}\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex44Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex44Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(p_{E}-p_{C})\,\bigl(\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\alpha_{C}^{(t)}\eta\,\mathbb{E}[D^{(t)}\mid\mathcal{F}_{t}]-K\eta^{2}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(p_{E}-p_{C})\,\bigl(\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\alpha_{C}^{(t)}\eta\,\mathbb{E}[D^{(t)}\mid\mathcal{F}_{t}]-K\eta^{2}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex44Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex44Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(p_{E}-p_{C})\,\bigl(\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\alpha_{C}^{(t)}\eta\gamma-K\eta^{2}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(p_{E}-p_{C})\,\bigl(\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\alpha_{C}^{(t)}\eta\gamma-K\eta^{2}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A5.SS4.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is the uniform score gap in Assumption <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem5" title="Assumption E.5 (Uniform score gap). ‣ E.4 Converting Potential Energy into Submartingale Drift ‣ Appendix E Theoretical Analysis of AceMAD ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.5</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choosing <math id="A5.SS4.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> small enough, e.g.</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leq\frac{\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\alpha_{C}^{(t)}\gamma}{2K}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leq\frac{\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\alpha_{C}^{(t)}\gamma}{2K},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">ensures that the bracketed term is non-negative, and strictly positive whenever <math id="A5.SS4.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\alpha_{C}^{(t)}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>C</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{E}^{(t)}\alpha_{C}^{(t)}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\bigl[p_{w}^{(t+1)}(Y=1)\,\big|\,\mathcal{F}_{t}\bigr]\geq p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\bigl[p_{w}^{(t+1)}(Y=1)\,\big|\,\mathcal{F}_{t}\bigr]\geq p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS4.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS4.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">with strict inequality as long as both agents retain non-zero weight share. This establishes the sub-martingale property and the strictly positive drift away from the initial state.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS4.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p14.1" class="ltx_p">By standard results on multiplicative weights and truth-holder advice, such a persistent score advantage implies that the truth-holder’s weight converges to one, and hence the aggregated belief <math id="A5.SS4.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{w}^{(t)}(Y=1)</annotation></semantics></math> converges to the truth-holder’s belief, which is itself close to the ground truth under the correlated noise assumptions.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Robustness Across Model Architectures</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To verify that AceMAD’s performance gains are not artifacts of specific model architectures or training procedures, we conduct additional experiments using <span id="A6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DeepSeek-V3.1</span>, a recent open-source model with different architectural design and pre-training data distribution compared to <span id="A6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GPT-4o-mini</span> and <span id="A6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen3</span>. The results in Table <a href="#A6.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix F Robustness Across Model Architectures ‣ Breaking the Martingale Curse: Multi-Agent Debate via Asymmetric Cognitive Potential Energy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> demonstrate that our peer-prediction mechanism successfully extracts asymmetric cognitive potential energy across diverse model families.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Notably, <span id="A6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DeepSeek-V3.1</span> achieves particularly strong baseline performance on several benchmarks (e.g., 75% on ARC-C with Majority Voting), suggesting that this model family may have less severe correlated noise in its default generation patterns. Nevertheless, AceMAD still provides consistent improvements (average +6.36%), with the most substantial gains observed on LogiQA (+6.87%) and BBH (+5.25%). This validates our theoretical claim that second-order belief elicitation is a model-agnostic mechanism for breaking the Martingale Curse, effective even when baseline error rates are relatively low.
The one exception is TruthfulQA,where AceMAD shows a slight degradation. We hypothesize this occurs because <span id="A6.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">DeepSeek-V3.1</span>’s strong factual knowledge reduces the presence of a “hallucinating majority” on this benchmark, causing peer predictions to become less informative. This pattern reinforces our framework’s scope: AceMAD is specifically designed for the Challenging Interval where correlated misconceptions dominate; in easier regimes where errors are independent, Decentralized MAD or even single-agent inference may suffice.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Generalization across models: Performance comparison using the <span id="A6.T4.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DeepSeek-V3.1</span> model (<math id="A6.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=5</annotation></semantics></math>). <span id="A6.T4.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">AceMAD</span> consistently outperforms all baseline variants, demonstrating its robustness across different LLM architectures.</figcaption>
